    "title": "Employee Arrested in Greenlawn Massage Parlor Raid - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Pam Robinson ,\n4 hours ago Suffolk County Police arrested a woman Wednesday on charges off unauthorized practice of a profession during a massage parlor raid in Greenlawn.\nOfficers from the Second Precinct Crime Unit officers, in conjunction with the Human Trafficking Unit, Town of Huntington Fire Marshal and Ordinance Inspector’s office, conducted an investigation into Valley Sole Spa, located at 51 Broadway, Unit 6, and arrested an employee.\nLianlin Liang, 47, of Flushing, was charged with Unauthorized Practice of a Profession, a Felony.\nThe Town of Huntington Fire Marshal and Code Enforcement Inspectors issued several violations to the business and is conducting a further investigation. Liang was issued a Desk Appearance ticket and is scheduled to appear in First District Court in Central Islip on a later date.\nIt was the second time in two months that the spa was raided. A worker with the same name and age was arrested there in March on charges of authorized practice of a profession and prostitution. She is due in court in June on that arrest.\nWorker Arrested at Valley Sole Spa in Greenlawn",
    "summary": "4 hours ago Suffolk County Police arrested a woman Wednesday on charges off unauthorized practice of a profession during a massage parlor raid in Greenlawn. Officers from the Second Precinct Crime Unit officers, in conjunction with the Human Trafficking Unit, Town of Huntington Fire Marshal and Ordinance Inspector’s office, conducted an investigation into Valley Sole Spa, located at 51 Broadway, Unit 6, and arrested an employee. Lianlin Liang, 47, of Flushing, was charged with Unauthorized Practice of a Profession, a Felony.",
